; std/loops: what a loop that gives a value fails with. A loop gives one
; without this module, `bind r = loop … fi`; a file that names `LoopResult`
; itself, in a type or a variant, brings it in with
; `include std/loops {LoopResult}`, or names `loops.LoopResult` after
; `include std/loops`.

; Why a loop that gives a value has none: `B` is what a `break = v` gives,
; and `M` what the last line's `fail LoopResult.Manual(m)` gives, `bool` where
; the loop gives none.
kind LoopResult<B, M>
    ; The body never ran: the condition failed at once, or there was nothing
    ; to go through.
    Skipped
    ; A `break` stopped it, with the value it gave, or `none`.
    Broke(value: maybe B)
    ; Its final pass ended with `continue`, before the last line.
    EndedByContinue
    ; The last line of the final pass failed with this.
    Manual(value: M)
fi
